## Reusable knowledge

- On this Meizu 20 / Flyme 12.5.0.0A build, the Qualcomm battery-driver controls were `/sys/class/qcom-battery/moisture
_detection_en` (read/write enable) and `/sys/class/qcom-battery/moisture_detection_status` (status). Before the change,
 both were `1`, battery was `Not charging`, logs included `moisture: Contaminant presence detected`, and `dumpsys usb` 
reported `contaminant_presence_status=detected`. [Task 1]
- Ordinary `adb shell` was UID 2000; Magisk being installed was insufficient. `/debug_ramdisk/su -c id` returned `uid=0
(root)` with `context=u:r:magisk:s0`, permitting the protected-node change. [Task 1]
- Writing `0` to `moisture_detection_en` yielded readback enable/status `0/0`, USB `contaminant_presence_status=not det
ected`, and battery `Not charging -> Charging`; the user confirmed "已经冲上电了". The prepared restoration script writ
es `1` through Magisk root and verifies its readback: `C:\Users\25011\Documents\codex\2026-11-01\wo\outputs\restore-mei
zu20-usb-detection.ps1`. [Task 1]
- This bypasses a hardware safety mechanism. Actual moisture or debris can create corrosion, heating, or damage risk; i
nspect/clean the port and restore protection after troubleshooting. [Task 1]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Symptom: `adb` is absent from PATH -> use official Platform-Tools and invoke its absolute `adb.exe`; this rollout use
d `work\android-diagnostic\platform-tools\adb.exe`. [Task 1]
- Symptom: ordinary shell cannot read/write the sysfs nodes -> explicitly verify `/debug_ramdisk/su -c id`; do not infe
r ADB root from Magisk UI presence. [Task 1]
- Symptom: nested PowerShell produces `Missing variable name after foreach` -> avoid fragile nested quoting; an encoded
 PowerShell command worked in this rollout. [Task 1]
- The setting was runtime-only and the device was not rebooted/reconnected because its battery was critically low. Do n
ot claim boot persistence or a Magisk boot script: only a restoration script was created. [Task 1]


