`startBackend()`. The 700ms value belongs to startup/reuse probing. `backendProcess.ts` can ultimately run `taskkill /P
ID ... /T /F` after 30 seconds and source review found no active-run guard. [Task 3]
- Keep service health, process liveness, and task state distinct. Public Codex App Server shows `/readyz`, `/healthz`, 
thread/turn/item lifecycle, per-turn `turn/interrupt`, and overload retry; OpenCode separates `/global/health`, SSE eve
nts, async prompt, and session abort. These prove public API patterns, not the complete Codex Desktop watchdog implemen
tation. [Task 3]

