ation, while fixtures timed out or aborted. Explicitly collect/test `-m 'unit or integration'`, isolate failures, and n
ever translate raw failure count directly into product-bug count. [Task 1]
- Symptom: cancellation test did not cancel when no `tool.output` arrived -> confirm the child process through API firs
t, then issue cancellation and verify `run.cancelled` plus process exit; UI events alone are not sufficient. [Task 1]
- Symptom: correct data result but an unrequested `audit.py` was created/deleted -> inspect process tool calls and file
 diffs as well as final output. A single prompt that cut calls from 15 to 6 is evidence of a possible policy/guide impr
ovement, not a stable performance ratio. [Task 1][Task 2]


